---
// The ZIP district map: sidebar (strategies, stats, ZIP search, district card, state table) + MapLibre map.
// Ported from the former public/standalone.html. Styles live in src/styles/map.css (global, unlayered).
import "../styles/map.css";

// site base with a trailing slash, for links to other pages (works under any `base`)
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
---
<div class="app">
  <aside>
    <header>
      <h1>All 435 districts</h1>
      <p class="lede">U.S. House districts redrawn by joining neighboring ZIP codes, with no voter or party data. Each state keeps its 2020 seat count and every district aims for that state's ideal population.</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="h-strat">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2 id="h-strat">Method</h2><span>ranked, most neutral first</span></div>
      <div class="modes" id="strategies" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="h-strat"></div>
      <button type="button" class="more" id="modes-more" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="strategies"></button>
      <p class="desc"><span id="strat-desc"></span> <a id="strat-more" href={`${base}methodology#modes`}>How it works →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="h-stats">
      <h2 id="h-stats">Balance, 429 districts in multi-seat states</h2>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat"><b id="st-mean">–</b><span>avg. deviation</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b id="st-max">–</b><span>largest</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b id="st-w1">–</b><span id="st-w1-l">within ±1%</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b id="st-cs">–</b><span>counties split</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <form class="row" id="zipform">
        <label for="zipq" class="vh">ZIP code</label>
        <input type="search" id="zipq" inputmode="numeric" maxlength="5" placeholder="Find a ZIP code" autocomplete="off">
        <button class="btn" type="submit" id="zipgo">Show</button>
      </form>
      <div class="hint" id="ziphint"></div>
    </section>

    <section id="selcard" aria-live="polite"></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="h-state">
      <h2 id="h-state">Districts by state</h2>
      <div class="selectwrap"><select id="statesel" aria-labelledby="h-state"></select></div>
      <div id="statetable" style="margin-top:8px"></div>
    </section>

    <details>
      <summary>Method and data</summary>
      <p><a href={`${base}methodology`}><b>Read the full methodology</b></a>: data, rules and a step-by-step explanation of every mode.</p>
      <p><b>Building blocks.</b> 33,585 ZIP Code Tabulation Areas (the Census Bureau's land-area version of ZIP codes) with 2020 Census population. ZIPs are never split, with one exception: state lines come first, so the 137 ZIPs that a state line runs through are split at that line, one piece per state, each with its own Census population.</p>
      <p><b>Seats and targets.</b> Each state keeps its 2020 apportionment. The national average is 761,169 people per seat, but districts cannot cross state lines, so the target is the state's population divided by its seats (Montana ≈ 542,000 per district, Delaware ≈ 990,000 for its single seat).</p>
      <p><b>Modes.</b> Listed from most to least defensible as a neutral rule: the fewer choices a person could tune, the higher the rank (<a href={`${base}methodology#ranking`}>why this order</a>). <i>Fixed rule</i> modes follow one mechanical rule. <i>Start point</i> modes grow districts outward from an anchor. <i>Pick by rule</i> modes choose among many possible maps using a rule set before any map was drawn, so nobody can keep redrawing until they like the result.</p>
      <p><b>Same finish for every mode.</b> After a mode draws its first version, a balancing pass trades border ZIPs between neighboring districts to even out population, keeping every district in one piece and its borders smooth.</p>
      <p><b>Random seed.</b> The random modes take their seed from a number published before any map existed: <span id="pubseed"></span>. Anyone can rerun the code and get identical maps.</p>
      <p><b>Counties split</b> counts counties whose ZIP areas fall in more than one district. Each ZIP area is assigned to the county holding most of its land.</p>
      <p><b>Neighbors.</b> ZIPs are neighbors when their boundaries touch, when they face each other across unpopulated land within 25 km, or across water when that is the only link (islands).</p>
      <p><b>Grey areas</b> are land with no ZIP code area (national forests, deserts, parks). They have no residents and belong to no district.</p>
      <p><b>Sources.</b> U.S. Census Bureau: 2020 DHC Table P1 by ZCTA; 2020 cartographic boundaries (cb_2020_us_zcta520_500k, county and state 500k); 2020 apportionment.</p>
    </details>
  </aside>

  <div id="map">
    <div class="mapctl">
      <div class="jump" role="group" aria-label="Jump to region">
        <button type="button" data-view="l48" id="v-l48">All 50 states</button>
        <button type="button" data-view="ak" id="v-ak">Alaska</button>
        <button type="button" data-view="hi" id="v-hi">Hawaii</button>
      </div>
      <div class="jump proj" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Map projection">
        <button type="button" role="radio" data-proj="globe" aria-checked="true" title="Globe: true north, the U.S. curves as on a reference map">Globe</button>
        <button type="button" role="radio" data-proj="mercator" aria-checked="false" title="Flat: Web Mercator, north is straight up everywhere">Flat</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="themepick" id="themepick">
      <button type="button" class="themebtn" id="themebtn" aria-haspopup="listbox" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="themelist"><span class="sws" id="themesw" aria-hidden="true"></span><span id="themename">Theme</span><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 4.5 6 8l3.5-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/></svg></button>
      <div class="themelist" id="themelist" role="listbox" aria-label="Map theme" tabindex="-1" hidden></div>
    </div>
    <div class="legend" id="legend">
      <button type="button" class="legend-toggle" id="legend-toggle" aria-expanded="true">Legend</button>
      <div class="li"><span class="k" id="lg-dist" style="opacity:.9"></span><span>District<small>Colors only tell neighbors apart.</small></span></div>
      <div class="li"><span class="k" id="lg-land"></span><span>No ZIP code area<small>Unpopulated land such as national forests, deserts and parks. Zero residents, so it belongs to no district.</small></span></div>
      <div class="li"><span class="k line" id="lg-state"></span><span>State line</span></div>
      <div class="li"><span class="k line thin" id="lg-border"></span><span>District border</span></div>
    </div>
    <!-- Alaska and Hawaii drawn below the Southwest, as on a reference map, so all 50 states fit in one view -->
    <div class="insets" id="insets" hidden>
      <div class="inset" id="inset-ak" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Alaska: select a district, or press Enter to zoom to Alaska"><div class="inset-map"></div></div>
      <div class="inset" id="inset-hi" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Hawaii: select a district, or press Enter to zoom to Hawaii"><div class="inset-map"></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tip" id="tip"></div>
    <div class="loading" id="loading"><div>Loading 33,585 ZIP code areas…<div class="bar"><i id="loadbar"></i></div></div></div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  // @ts-nocheck -- ported near line for line from the standalone page's plain-JS script; not typed (yet).
  import maplibregl from "maplibre-gl";
  import "maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css";
  import * as topojson from "topojson-client";
  import { THEMES, DEFAULT_THEME, themeById } from "../lib/themes.js";

  // map theme (colours only): remembered per browser; "?theme=<id>" in the URL overrides it
  let TH = themeById(DEFAULT_THEME);
  try { TH = themeById(new URLSearchParams(location.search).get("theme") || localStorage.getItem("zd-theme") || DEFAULT_THEME); } catch (e) {}
  const pal = (i) => TH.fills[i] ?? "#999999";
  const widths = (stops, k) => ["interpolate", ["linear"], ["zoom"], ...stops.flatMap(([z, w]) => [z, +(w * k).toFixed(2)])];
  const DIST_W = [[3, 0.4], [7, 1.2], [11, 2.4]], STATE_W = [[3, 1], [7, 2.4], [11, 3.6]];
  // projection: "globe" (default; true north, the U.S. curves like a conic reference map, flattening as you zoom in)
  // or "mercator" (flat). Remembered per browser.
  // default: Flat on phones (more of the map on a small screen), Globe elsewhere; a saved choice wins
  let PROJ = window.innerWidth < 760 ? "mercator" : "globe";
  try { const saved = localStorage.getItem("zd-proj"); if (saved === "mercator" || saved === "globe") PROJ = saved; } catch (e) {}
  const VIEWS = { l48: [[-127, 17], [-66.8, 49.5]], ak: [[-170, 51], [-129.5, 71.5]], hi: [[-160.5, 18.8], [-154.6, 22.4]] };
  const NAMES = {AL:"Alabama",AK:"Alaska",AZ:"Arizona",AR:"Arkansas",CA:"California",CO:"Colorado",CT:"Connecticut",DE:"Delaware",FL:"Florida",GA:"Georgia",HI:"Hawaii",ID:"Idaho",IL:"Illinois",IN:"Indiana",IA:"Iowa",KS:"Kansas",KY:"Kentucky",LA:"Louisiana",ME:"Maine",MD:"Maryland",MA:"Massachusetts",MI:"Michigan",MN:"Minnesota",MS:"Mississippi",MO:"Missouri",MT:"Montana",NE:"Nebraska",NV:"Nevada",NH:"New Hampshire",NJ:"New Jersey",NM:"New Mexico",NY:"New York",NC:"North Carolina",ND:"North Dakota",OH:"Ohio",OK:"Oklahoma",OR:"Oregon",PA:"Pennsylvania",RI:"Rhode Island",SC:"South Carolina",SD:"South Dakota",TN:"Tennessee",TX:"Texas",UT:"Utah",VT:"Vermont",VA:"Virginia",WA:"Washington",WV:"West Virginia",WI:"Wisconsin",WY:"Wyoming"};
  // data folder relative to the site base, so fetches work from any route
  const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
  const DATA = BASE + "data/";
  const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
  const fmt = (n) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString("en-US");
  const devClass = (d) => (Math.abs(d) <= 1 ? "good" : Math.abs(d) <= 2 ? "warn" : "bad");
  const devText = (d) => (d > 0 ? "+" : d < 0 ? "−" : "±") + Math.abs(d).toFixed(2) + "%";

  let S = location.hash.slice(1);   // validated against the mode list once data loads; default = top-ranked mode
  let attachModes, meta, topo, zctaFC, distFC = {}, lblFC = {}, zipIndex = new Map(), zipParts = new Map(), distBBox = {}, distZips = {};
  // A ZIP split by a state line is stored as one piece per state, with ids like "42223-TN"; whole ZIPs keep their 5 digits.
  const zipOf = (id) => id.slice(0, 5);
  const zipLabel = (id) => (id.length > 5 ? `${zipOf(id)} (${id.slice(6)} part)` : id);
  let selected = null, pinnedZip = null, markers = [], stateBBox = {}, selFilter = ["==", ["get", "zcta"], "__none__"], zipFilter = selFilter;
  const EMPTY = { type: "FeatureCollection", features: [] }, NONE = ["==", ["get", "zcta"], "__none__"];
  const DETAIL_Z = 7; const detail = { loaded: new Set(), loading: new Set(), z: [], d: [] };

  const css = (v) => getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue(v).trim();
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: "map",
    // globe projection: at national zoom the U.S. curves with true north, like a conic reference map; it flattens to
    // Mercator automatically as you zoom in. The space around the globe shows #map's background (the theme's ground).
    style: { version: 8, projection: { type: PROJ }, sources: {}, layers: [{ id: "bg", type: "background", paint: { "background-color": TH.ground } }] },
    bounds: VIEWS.l48, fitBoundsOptions: { padding: 20 }, maxZoom: 13.5, minZoom: 1, dragRotate: false, pitchWithRotate: false,
    attributionControl: { compact: true, customAttribution: "Boundaries & population: U.S. Census Bureau (2020)" },
  });
  map.touchZoomRotate.disableRotation();
  if (import.meta.env.DEV) window.__zd = { map, INSETS: () => INSETS }; // dev-only handle for debugging
  map.addControl(new maplibregl.NavigationControl({ showCompass: false }), "top-right");
  // reset button under + / −: back to the national view (same as "All 50 states")
  map.addControl({
    onAdd() {
      const el = document.createElement("div"); el.className = "maplibregl-ctrl maplibregl-ctrl-group";
      el.innerHTML = `<button type="button" class="zd-reset" title="Reset zoom: all 50 states" aria-label="Reset zoom to all 50 states"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 6V2.5H6M13.5 6V2.5H10M2.5 10v3.5H6M13.5 10v3.5H10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/></svg></button>`;
      el.querySelector("button").addEventListener("click", () => map.easeTo({ ...nationalCamera(), duration: 700 }));
      return el;
    },
    onRemove() {},
  }, "top-right");

  async function fetchWithProgress(url, onProg) {
    const res = await fetch(url);
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(url + " " + res.status);
    const total = +res.headers.get("content-length") || 0;
    if (!res.body || !total) return res.json();
    const reader = res.body.getReader(); const chunks = []; let got = 0;
    for (;;) { const { done, value } = await reader.read(); if (done) break; chunks.push(value); got += value.length; onProg(got / total); }
    const buf = new Uint8Array(got); let o = 0; for (const c of chunks) { buf.set(c, o); o += c.length; }
    return JSON.parse(new TextDecoder().decode(buf));
  }

  function bboxOf(geom, b = [180, 90, -180, -90]) {
    const walk = (c) => { if (typeof c[0] === "number") { if (c[0] < b[0]) b[0] = c[0]; if (c[1] < b[1]) b[1] = c[1]; if (c[0] > b[2]) b[2] = c[0]; if (c[1] > b[3]) b[3] = c[1]; } else c.forEach(walk); };
    walk(geom.coordinates); return b;
  }

  async function load() {
    const [m, modes, landTopo, t] = await Promise.all([
      fetch(DATA + "districts.json").then((r) => r.json()),
      fetch(DATA + "modes.json").then((r) => r.json()),
      fetch(DATA + "land.topo.json").then((r) => r.json()),
      fetchWithProgress(DATA + "zipdistricts.topo.json", (p) => ($("loadbar").style.width = Math.round(p * 100) + "%")),
    ]);
    meta = m; topo = t;
    if (!meta.strategies[S]) S = Object.keys(meta.strategies)[0];
    // attach every mode's district id + colour to each ZIP feature (kept out of the geometry files)
    const zi = new Map(modes.zctas.map((z, i) => [z, i])), MODES = Object.keys(modes.modes);
    attachModes = (f, st) => {
      const i = zi.get(f.properties.zcta); if (i === undefined) return;
      for (const s of MODES) { f.properties["d_" + s] = st + "-" + modes.modes[s].d[i]; f.properties["c_" + s] = modes.modes[s].c[i]; }
    };
    zctaFC = topojson.feature(topo, topo.objects.zctas);
    for (const f of zctaFC.features) attachModes(f, f.properties.st);
    for (const f of zctaFC.features) { const id = f.properties.zcta; zipIndex.set(id, f); (zipParts.get(zipOf(id)) ?? zipParts.set(zipOf(id), []).get(zipOf(id))).push(id); }
    for (const s of Object.keys(meta.strategies)) {
      distFC[s] = topojson.feature(topo, topo.objects["dist_" + s]);
      lblFC[s] = topojson.feature(topo, topo.objects["lbl_" + s]);
      distBBox[s] = {}; for (const f of distFC[s].features) distBBox[s][f.properties["d_" + s]] = bboxOf(f.geometry);
      const dz = (distZips[s] = {}); for (const f of zctaFC.features) (dz[f.properties["d_" + s]] ??= []).push(f.properties.zcta);
    }
    const states = topojson.feature(topo, topo.objects.states);
    if (!map.isStyleLoaded()) await new Promise((r) => map.once("load", r));
    stateBBox = Object.fromEntries(states.features.map((f) => [f.properties.st, bboxOf(f.geometry)]));
    map.addSource("zctas", { type: "geojson", data: zctaFC, tolerance: 0.25 });
    map.addSource("dist", { type: "geojson", data: distFC[S], tolerance: 0.25 });
    // state lines: only the borders BETWEEN states, from the Census boundaries (the ZIP-derived state shapes have
    // holes wherever there is no ZIP area, which would ring every patch of empty land)
    map.addSource("states", { type: "geojson", data: topojson.mesh(landTopo, landTopo.objects.land, (a, b) => a !== b), tolerance: 0.25 });
    // real Census state boundaries: covers land with no ZIP area (the ZIP-derived outlines have holes there)
    map.addSource("land", { type: "geojson", data: topojson.feature(landTopo, landTopo.objects.land), tolerance: 0.2 });
    map.addSource("zd", { type: "geojson", data: EMPTY, tolerance: 0.15 });
    map.addSource("dd", { type: "geojson", data: EMPTY, tolerance: 0.15 });
    const fillPaint = () => ({ "fill-color": fillExpr(), "fill-opacity": 0.78, "fill-antialias": false });
    const zipLinePaint = { "line-color": TH.border, "line-width": ["interpolate", ["linear"], ["zoom"], 6.5, 0.2, 11, 0.9], "line-opacity": ["interpolate", ["linear"], ["zoom"], 6.5, 0, 8, 0.55] };
    const distLinePaint = { "line-color": TH.border, "line-width": widths(DIST_W, TH.bw), "line-opacity": 1 };
    const selFill = { "fill-color": "#ffffff", "fill-opacity": 0.22 };
    const selLine = { "line-color": TH.sel, "line-width": ["interpolate", ["linear"], ["zoom"], 3, 2, 10, 4.5] };
    // coarse national layers (always loaded) …
    map.addLayer({ id: "land", type: "fill", source: "land", paint: { "fill-color": TH.land } });
    map.addLayer({ id: "zcta-fill", type: "fill", source: "zctas", paint: fillPaint() });
    map.addLayer({ id: "zcta-line", type: "line", source: "zctas", minzoom: 6.5, paint: zipLinePaint });
    // … and full-resolution layers for states in view once zoomed in
    map.addLayer({ id: "zd-fill", type: "fill", source: "zd", paint: fillPaint(), layout: { visibility: "none" } });
    map.addLayer({ id: "zd-line", type: "line", source: "zd", paint: zipLinePaint, layout: { visibility: "none" } });
    map.addLayer({ id: "sel-fill", type: "fill", source: "dist", filter: NONE, paint: selFill });
    map.addLayer({ id: "dd-sel-fill", type: "fill", source: "dd", filter: NONE, paint: selFill });
    map.addLayer({ id: "dist-line", type: "line", source: "dist", paint: distLinePaint });
    map.addLayer({ id: "dd-line", type: "line", source: "dd", filter: ["==", ["get", "s"], S], paint: distLinePaint, layout: { visibility: "none" } });
    map.addLayer({ id: "state-line", type: "line", source: "states", paint: { "line-color": TH.state, "line-width": widths(STATE_W, TH.sw) } });
    map.addLayer({ id: "sel-line", type: "line", source: "dist", filter: NONE, paint: selLine });
    map.addLayer({ id: "dd-sel-line", type: "line", source: "dd", filter: NONE, paint: selLine });
    map.addLayer({ id: "zip-line", type: "line", source: "zctas", filter: NONE, paint: { "line-color": TH.sel, "line-width": 2.2, "line-dasharray": [2, 1] } });
    map.addLayer({ id: "zd-zip-line", type: "line", source: "zd", filter: NONE, paint: { "line-color": TH.sel, "line-width": 2.2, "line-dasharray": [2, 1] } });
    buildInsets(topojson.feature(landTopo, landTopo.objects.land));
    $("loading").remove();
    buildStrategies();
    buildThemePicker();
    applyTheme(TH, true);
    $("pubseed").textContent = "“" + meta.publicSeed + "”";
    buildStateSelect();
    setStrategy(S, true);
    wireMap();
  }

  function fillExpr() {
    const e = ["match", ["get", "c_" + S]]; TH.fills.forEach((c, i) => e.push(i, c)); e.push("#999999"); return e;
  }

  // ranked method list (engine order = most to least neutral); the top TOP show, the rest behind "Show more"
  const TOP = 4;
  function buildStrategies() {
    const el = $("strategies"), ids = Object.keys(meta.strategies);
    el.innerHTML = ids.map((id, i) => { const info = meta.strategies[id];
      return `<button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="mode${i >= TOP ? " extra" : ""}" data-s="${id}" id="s-${id}" tabindex="-1"><span class="rank">${i + 1}</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="mode-name">${info.label}</span><span class="tag">${info.group}</span></button>`; }).join("");
    el.querySelectorAll("button").forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => setStrategy(b.dataset.s)));
    el.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => { // radio-group arrow keys
      const k = { ArrowDown: 1, ArrowRight: 1, ArrowUp: -1, ArrowLeft: -1 }[e.key]; if (!k) return;
      e.preventDefault(); const next = ids[(ids.indexOf(S) + k + ids.length) % ids.length]; setStrategy(next); $("s-" + next).focus();
    });
    const more = $("modes-more"), extra = ids.length - TOP;
    const setOpen = (open) => { el.classList.toggle("open", open); more.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(open)); more.textContent = open ? "Show fewer methods" : `Show ${extra} more methods`; };
    setOpen(false);
    more.addEventListener("click", () => setOpen(!el.classList.contains("open")));
    el._setOpen = setOpen;
  }

  // ---- map themes ----
  function buildThemePicker() {
    const list = $("themelist"), btn = $("themebtn"), groups = [...new Set(THEMES.map((t) => t.group))];
    list.innerHTML = groups.map((g) => { const ts = THEMES.filter((t) => t.group === g); return (ts.length === 1 && ts[0].name === g ? "" : `<div class="tgrp" role="presentation">${g}</div>`) + ts.map((t) =>
      `<button type="button" role="option" aria-selected="false" data-t="${t.id}" tabindex="-1"><span class="sws" aria-hidden="true">${t.fills.map((c) => `<i style="background:${c}"></i>`).join("")}</span><span class="tn"><b>${t.name}</b><small>${t.desc}</small></span><svg class="tick" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3.5 8.5 6.5 11.5 12.5 4.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg></button>`).join(""); }).join("");
    const opts = () => [...list.querySelectorAll("button")];
    const open = (o) => { list.hidden = !o; btn.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(o)); if (o) (list.querySelector('[aria-selected="true"]') || opts()[0]).focus(); };
    btn.addEventListener("click", () => open(list.hidden));
    list.addEventListener("click", (e) => { const b = e.target.closest("button[data-t]"); if (!b) return; applyTheme(themeById(b.dataset.t)); open(false); btn.focus(); });
    list.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
      const o = opts(), i = o.indexOf(document.activeElement);
      if (e.key === "Escape") { open(false); btn.focus(); }
      else if (e.key === "ArrowDown" || e.key === "ArrowUp") { e.preventDefault(); o[(i + (e.key === "ArrowDown" ? 1 : -1) + o.length) % o.length].focus(); }
    });
    document.addEventListener("click", (e) => { if (!list.hidden && !$("themepick").contains(e.target)) open(false); });
  }

  function applyTheme(t, initial) {
    TH = t;
    try { if (!initial) localStorage.setItem("zd-theme", t.id); } catch (e) {}
    const mapEl = $("map"); mapEl.dataset.mapTheme = t.id; mapEl.classList.toggle("dark-map", t.dark); mapEl.style.setProperty("--map-ground", t.ground);
    map.setPaintProperty("bg", "background-color", t.ground);
    map.setPaintProperty("bg", "background-opacity", t.stars ? 0 : 1); // Lunar: the CSS starfield shows through
    map.setPaintProperty("land", "fill-color", t.land);
    for (const L of ["zcta-fill", "zd-fill"]) map.setPaintProperty(L, "fill-color", fillExpr());
    for (const L of ["zcta-line", "zd-line"]) map.setPaintProperty(L, "line-color", t.border);
    for (const L of ["dist-line", "dd-line"]) { map.setPaintProperty(L, "line-color", t.border); map.setPaintProperty(L, "line-width", widths(DIST_W, t.bw)); }
    map.setPaintProperty("state-line", "line-color", t.state); map.setPaintProperty("state-line", "line-width", widths(STATE_W, t.sw));
    for (const L of ["sel-line", "dd-sel-line", "zip-line", "zd-zip-line"]) map.setPaintProperty(L, "line-color", t.sel);
    for (const L of ["sel-fill", "dd-sel-fill"]) map.setPaintProperty(L, "fill-opacity", t.dark ? 0.16 : 0.3);
    $("themename").textContent = t.name; $("themebtn").setAttribute("aria-label", "Map theme: " + t.name);
    $("themesw").innerHTML = t.fills.slice(0, 3).map((c) => `<i style="background:${c}"></i>`).join("");
    $("themelist").querySelectorAll("button").forEach((b) => b.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(b.dataset.t === t.id)));
    const f = t.fills;
    $("lg-dist").style.background = `linear-gradient(90deg, ${f[0]} 0 20%, ${f[1]} 20% 40%, ${f[2]} 40% 60%, ${f[3]} 60% 80%, ${f[4]} 80%)`;
    $("lg-land").style.background = t.land;
    $("lg-state").style.background = `linear-gradient(180deg, ${t.ground} 0 40%, ${t.state} 40% 60%, ${t.ground} 60%)`;
    $("lg-border").style.background = `linear-gradient(90deg, ${f[0]} 0 44%, ${t.border} 44% 56%, ${f[1]} 56%)`;
    styleInsets();
    if (!initial) { renderCard(); renderStateTable(); }
  }

  function setStrategy(s, initial) {
    S = s;
    if (!initial || location.hash.slice(1) !== s) history.replaceState(null, "", "#" + s);
    document.querySelectorAll("#strategies button").forEach((b) => { const on = b.dataset.s === s; b.setAttribute("aria-checked", String(on)); b.tabIndex = on ? 0 : -1; });
    if (Object.keys(meta.strategies).indexOf(s) >= TOP) $("strategies")._setOpen(true);
    const grp = document.createElement("b"); grp.textContent = meta.strategies[s].group + ". ";
    $("strat-desc").replaceChildren(grp, meta.strategies[s].desc);
    $("strat-more").href = BASE + "methodology#mode-" + s;
    const sum = meta.results[s].summary;
    $("st-mean").textContent = sum.meanAbsDevPct.toFixed(2) + "%";
    $("st-max").textContent = sum.maxAbsDevPct.toFixed(1) + "%";
    $("st-w1").textContent = sum.within1pct; $("st-w1-l").textContent = `of ${sum.multiSeatDistricts} within ±1%`;
    $("st-cs").textContent = sum.countySplits.toLocaleString("en-US");
    map.setPaintProperty("zcta-fill", "fill-color", fillExpr());
    map.setPaintProperty("zd-fill", "fill-color", fillExpr());
    map.setFilter("dd-line", ["==", ["get", "s"], s]);
    map.getSource("dist").setData(distFC[s]);
    styleInsets(true);
    // keep the same place selected: follow the pinned ZIP, or the old district's first ZIP
    let anchorZip = pinnedZip || (selected && distZips[prevS]?.[selected]?.[0]);
    prevS = s;
    select(anchorZip ? zipIndex.get(anchorZip).properties["d_" + s] : null, false);
    renderStateTable();
    updateLabels();
    if (!initial) refreshDetail();
  }
  let prevS = S;

  function select(id, fly = true) {
    selected = id;
    const f = ["==", ["get", "d_" + S], id || "__none__"];
    const fd = ["all", ["==", ["get", "s"], S], ["==", ["get", "d"], id || "__none__"]];
    selFilter = f; refreshDetail();
    map.setFilter("dd-sel-fill", fd); map.setFilter("dd-sel-line", fd);
    for (const { m, loaded } of Object.values(INSETS)) if (loaded) m.setFilter("sel-line", f);
    renderCard();
    renderStateTable();
    if (id && fly) map.fitBounds(distBBox[S][id], { padding: 50, maxZoom: 10.5, duration: 700 });
  }

  function renderCard() {
    const el = $("selcard");
    if (!selected) { el.innerHTML = ""; return; }
    const [pop, dev, nz] = meta.results[S].districts[selected];
    const st = selected.split("-")[0];
    const f = distFC[S].features.find((x) => x.properties["d_" + S] === selected);
    const color = pal(f ? f.properties["c_" + S] : 0);
    const zips = (distZips[S][selected] || []).slice().sort();
    el.innerHTML = `<div class="card">
      <div class="title"><b><span class="sw" style="background:${color}"></span>${selected}</b><span class="pill ${devClass(dev)}">${devText(dev)} vs ideal</span></div>
      <dl class="kv">
        <dt>State</dt><dd>${NAMES[st]} · ${meta.seats[st]} seat${meta.seats[st] > 1 ? "s" : ""}</dd>
        <dt>Population (2020)</dt><dd>${fmt(pop)}</dd>
        <dt>State ideal</dt><dd>${fmt(meta.ideal[st])}</dd>
        <dt>ZIP codes</dt><dd>${nz}</dd>
      </dl>
      <div class="zips" aria-label="ZIP codes in ${selected}">${zips.map((z) => `<button type="button" data-zip="${z}" ${z === pinnedZip ? 'style="border-color:var(--accent)"' : ""}>${zipLabel(z)}</button>`).join("")}</div>
    </div>`;
    el.querySelectorAll(".zips button").forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => showZip(b.dataset.zip)));
  }

  function buildStateSelect() {
    const sel = $("statesel");
    sel.innerHTML = Object.keys(meta.seats).sort((a, b) => NAMES[a].localeCompare(NAMES[b])).map((st) => `<option value="${st}">${NAMES[st]} (${meta.seats[st]})</option>`).join("");
    sel.value = "IL";
    sel.addEventListener("change", () => {
      renderStateTable();
      const ids = Object.keys(distBBox[S]).filter((d) => d.startsWith(sel.value + "-"));
      const b = ids.reduce((a, d) => { const x = distBBox[S][d]; return [Math.min(a[0], x[0]), Math.min(a[1], x[1]), Math.max(a[2], x[2]), Math.max(a[3], x[3])]; }, [180, 90, -180, -90]);
      map.fitBounds(b, { padding: 30, duration: 700 });
    });
  }

  function renderStateTable() {
    const st = selected ? selected.split("-")[0] : $("statesel").value;
    if ($("statesel").value !== st) $("statesel").value = st;
    const n = meta.seats[st]; const rows = [];
    const colorOf = {}; for (const f of distFC[S].features) colorOf[f.properties["d_" + S]] = f.properties["c_" + S];
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      const id = `${st}-${i}`; const [pop, dev, nz] = meta.results[S].districts[id];
      rows.push(`<tr data-id="${id}" tabindex="0" class="${id === selected ? "sel" : ""}"><td><span class="sw" style="background:${pal(colorOf[id])}"></span>${i}</td><td class="num">${fmt(pop)}</td><td class="num"><span class="pill ${devClass(dev)}">${devText(dev)}</span></td><td class="num">${nz}</td></tr>`);
    }
    $("statetable").innerHTML = `<table><thead><tr><th>District</th><th class="num">Population</th><th class="num">vs ideal</th><th class="num">ZIPs</th></tr></thead><tbody>${rows.join("")}</tbody></table>
      <div class="hint">Ideal for ${NAMES[st]}: ${fmt(meta.ideal[st])} people per district · ${meta.stateStats[S][st].countySplits} counties split${S === "best" && meta.seats[st] > 1 ? ` · winning map: <b>${meta.strategies[meta.stateStats.best[st].winner].label}</b>` : ""}</div>`;
    $("statetable").querySelectorAll("tbody tr").forEach((tr) => {
      tr.addEventListener("click", () => select(tr.dataset.id));
      tr.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => { if (e.key === "Enter") select(tr.dataset.id); });
    });
  }

  // z: a 5-digit ZIP (all of its pieces) or one piece id ("42223-TN")
  function showZip(z) {
    const ids = zipIndex.has(z) ? [z] : zipParts.get(z) ?? [];
    if (!ids.length) { $("ziphint").textContent = `${z} isn't a populated ZIP area in the 50 states. Try a nearby residential ZIP.`; return; }
    const fs = ids.map((id) => zipIndex.get(id)).sort((a, b) => b.properties.pop - a.properties.pop);
    const f = fs[0];
    pinnedZip = f.properties.zcta;
    zipFilter = ["in", ["get", "zcta"], ["literal", ids]]; map.setFilter("zd-zip-line", zipFilter); refreshDetail();
    const all = zipParts.get(zipOf(z)) ?? ids;
    $("ziphint").textContent = all.length > 1 && ids.length > 1
      ? `${zipOf(z)} is split by a state line: ` + fs.map((x) => `${x.properties.zcta.slice(6)} part, ${fmt(x.properties.pop)} people → ${x.properties["d_" + S]}`).join(" · ")
      : `${zipLabel(f.properties.zcta)} · ${fmt(f.properties.pop)} people · district ${f.properties["d_" + S]}`;
    select(f.properties["d_" + S], false);
    const b = fs.map((x) => bboxOf(x.geometry)).reduce((a, x) => [Math.min(a[0], x[0]), Math.min(a[1], x[1]), Math.max(a[2], x[2]), Math.max(a[3], x[3])]);
    map.fitBounds(b, { padding: 120, maxZoom: 11, duration: 700 });
  }

  // ---- full-resolution state files, fetched on demand when zoomed in ----
  function statesInView() {
    const b = map.getBounds(); const v = [b.getWest(), b.getSouth(), b.getEast(), b.getNorth()];
    return Object.entries(stateBBox).filter(([, x]) => x[0] < v[2] && x[2] > v[0] && x[1] < v[3] && x[3] > v[1]).map(([st]) => st);
  }
  function loadDetail() {
    if (map.getZoom() < DETAIL_Z - 0.5) return;
    for (const st of statesInView()) {
      if (detail.loaded.has(st) || detail.loading.has(st)) continue;
      detail.loading.add(st);
      fetch(DATA + "states/" + st + ".topo.json").then((r) => r.json()).then((t) => {
        for (const f of topojson.feature(t, t.objects.zctas).features) { f.properties.st = st; attachModes(f, st); detail.z.push(f); }
        for (const s of Object.keys(meta.strategies)) for (const f of topojson.feature(t, t.objects["dist_" + s]).features) {
          f.properties = { s, d: f.properties["d_" + s] }; detail.d.push(f);
        }
        detail.loaded.add(st); detail.loading.delete(st);
        map.getSource("zd").setData({ type: "FeatureCollection", features: detail.z });
        map.getSource("dd").setData({ type: "FeatureCollection", features: detail.d });
        refreshDetail();
      }).catch(() => detail.loading.delete(st));
    }
  }
  function refreshDetail() {
    const on = map.getZoom() >= DETAIL_Z && detail.loaded.size > 0;
    for (const L of ["zd-fill", "zd-line", "dd-line"]) map.setLayoutProperty(L, "visibility", on ? "visible" : "none");
    const loaded = ["literal", [...detail.loaded]];
    // hide coarse shapes wherever the detailed version is showing
    map.setFilter("zcta-fill", on ? ["!", ["in", ["get", "st"], loaded]] : null);
    map.setFilter("zcta-line", on ? ["!", ["in", ["get", "st"], loaded]] : null);
    const notLoadedD = ["!", ["in", ["slice", ["get", "d_" + S], 0, 2], loaded]];
    map.setFilter("dist-line", on ? notLoadedD : null);
    map.setFilter("sel-fill", on ? ["all", selFilter, notLoadedD] : selFilter);
    map.setFilter("sel-line", on ? ["all", selFilter, notLoadedD] : selFilter);
    map.setFilter("zip-line", on ? ["all", zipFilter, ["!", ["in", ["get", "st"], loaded]]] : zipFilter);
  }

  // ---- Alaska / Hawaii insets: two small non-interactive maps drawn into empty space below the Southwest, like a printed
  // reference map (no frames). Each sits in a fixed lon/lat "slot" of the main map, so it pans and zooms with the map.
  // They show only at (or near) the national view and when the main map isn't already showing that state.
  // what each inset shows (mainland Alaska with most of the Aleutians; the main Hawaiian islands)
  const INSET_FIT = { ak: [[-172, 51.5], [-130, 71.4]], hi: [[-160.6, 18.8], [-154.7, 22.3]] };
  // fitBounds is approximate on the globe at low zoom, so fit by measuring the projected outline and correcting the zoom
  const INSET_PTS = {}; // sampled outline points of each state's land, filled in buildInsets
  function fitInset(m, [[w0, s0], [e0, n0]], W, H, pts) {
    // start from the same camera every time (no drift), then alternately re-centre on the shape and correct the zoom
    m.jumpTo({ center: [(w0 + e0) / 2, (s0 + n0) / 2], zoom: Math.log2(360 / (e0 - w0)) + Math.log2(W / 512) });
    for (let k = 0; k < 5; k++) {
      const ps = pts.map((p) => m.project(p)), xs = ps.map((p) => p.x), ys = ps.map((p) => p.y);
      const x0 = Math.min(...xs), x1 = Math.max(...xs), y0 = Math.min(...ys), y1 = Math.max(...ys);
      m.jumpTo({ center: m.unproject([(x0 + x1) / 2, (y0 + y1) / 2]), zoom: m.getZoom() + Math.log2(Math.min(W / (x1 - x0), H / (y1 - y0))) });
    }
    // sit the shape on the bottom edge of its box (the line through the southern tip of Texas)
    const maxY = Math.max(...pts.map((p) => m.project(p).y));
    m.jumpTo({ center: m.unproject([W / 2, H / 2 - (H - maxY)]) });
  }
  // Per projection: on the flat (Mercator) map the gap below California is shallower, so the insets are smaller.
  const LAYOUTS = {
    globe: { ak: { x0: 0.02, x1: 0.25, h: 0.3 }, hi: { x0: 0.235, x1: 0.37, h: 0.13 } },
    mercator: { ak: { x0: 0, x1: 0.2, h: 0.2 }, hi: { x0: 0.215, x1: 0.34, h: 0.11 } },
  };
  const L48 = [[-124.8, 24.4], [-66.9, 49.4]], TX_TIP = [-97.4, 25.84];
  const L48_PTS = []; for (let i = 0; i <= 12; i++) { const x = L48[0][0] + ((L48[1][0] - L48[0][0]) * i) / 12, y = L48[0][1] + ((L48[1][1] - L48[0][1]) * i) / 12; L48_PTS.push([x, L48[0][1]], [x, L48[1][1]], [L48[0][0], y], [L48[1][0], y]); }
  function l48Frame() {
    const ps = L48_PTS.map((p) => map.project(p)), xs = ps.map((p) => p.x), ys = ps.map((p) => p.y);
    return { x0: Math.min(...xs), x1: Math.max(...xs), y0: Math.min(...ys), y1: Math.max(...ys), base: map.project(TX_TIP).y };
  }
  let NAT = null, measuring = false;
  function nationalCamera() {
    if (NAT) return NAT;
    measuring = true; // the jumps below fire "move"; updateInsets must ignore them
    const keep = { center: map.getCenter(), zoom: map.getZoom() };
    // room for the buttons along the top (PT) and a margin elsewhere
    const W = map.getContainer().clientWidth, H = map.getContainer().clientHeight;
    const PX = W < 500 ? 14 : 36, PT = W < 500 ? 60 : 72, PB = W < 500 ? 24 : 40;
    map.jumpTo({ center: [-96, 37], zoom: 3 });
    for (let k = 0; k < 4; k++) {
      const f = l48Frame();
      // move the frame's centre to the centre of the free area (which sits lower than the canvas centre when PT > PB)
      const c = map.unproject([(f.x0 + f.x1) / 2, (f.y0 + f.y1) / 2 - (PT - PB) / 2]);
      map.jumpTo({ center: c, zoom: map.getZoom() + Math.log2(Math.min((W - 2 * PX) / (f.x1 - f.x0), (H - PT - PB) / (f.y1 - f.y0))) });
    }
    NAT = { center: map.getCenter(), zoom: map.getZoom() };
    map.jumpTo(keep);
    measuring = false;
    return NAT;
  }
  // Click a district to select it (the main map flies there); Enter zooms the main map to the state.
  const INSETS = {};
  const distOf = (st) => ({ type: "FeatureCollection", features: distFC[S].features.filter((f) => f.properties["d_" + S].startsWith(st + "-")) });
  function buildInsets(landFC) {
    for (const [key, st] of [["ak", "AK"], ["hi", "HI"]]) {
      const el = $("inset-" + key);
      const m = new maplibregl.Map({
        container: el.querySelector(".inset-map"), interactive: false, attributionControl: false, fadeDuration: 0,
        style: { version: 8, projection: { type: PROJ }, sources: {}, layers: [] }, // transparent: the main map shows through
        bounds: VIEWS[key], fitBoundsOptions: { padding: 0 },
      });
      const inset = (INSETS[key] = { m, st, loaded: false });
      // outline points for fitting (Alaska: only the western hemisphere, so islands past 180° don't stretch the fit)
      // Alaska: western hemisphere only (islands past 180° would stretch the fit); Hawaii: the eight main islands
      // (the uninhabited Northwestern islands reach 178°W and would shrink the main islands to dots)
      const keep = st === "HI" ? (c) => c[0] > -160.6 : (c) => c[0] < 0;
      const pts = []; const walk = (c) => { if (typeof c[0] === "number") { if (keep(c)) pts.push(c); } else c.forEach(walk); };
      for (const f of landFC.features) if (f.properties.STUSPS === st) walk(f.geometry.coordinates);
      INSET_PTS[key] = pts.filter((_, i) => i % 4 === 0);
      m.once("load", () => {
        m.addSource("land", { type: "geojson", data: { type: "FeatureCollection", features: landFC.features.filter((f) => f.properties.STUSPS === st) } });
        m.addSource("dist", { type: "geojson", data: distOf(st) });
        m.addLayer({ id: "land", type: "fill", source: "land", paint: { "fill-color": TH.land } });
        m.addLayer({ id: "dist-fill", type: "fill", source: "dist", paint: { "fill-color": fillExpr(), "fill-opacity": 0.78 } });
        m.addLayer({ id: "dist-line", type: "line", source: "dist", paint: { "line-color": TH.border, "line-width": 0.7 } });
        m.addLayer({ id: "sel-line", type: "line", source: "dist", filter: selFilter, paint: { "line-color": TH.sel, "line-width": 2 } });
        inset.loaded = true; styleInsets();
      });
      el.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
        const r = m.getCanvas().getBoundingClientRect();
        const f = inset.loaded && m.queryRenderedFeatures([e.clientX - r.left, e.clientY - r.top], { layers: ["dist-fill"] })[0];
        if (f) { pinnedZip = null; zipFilter = NONE; map.setFilter("zd-zip-line", NONE); select(f.properties["d_" + S]); }
        else map.fitBounds(VIEWS[key], { padding: 20, duration: 700 });
      });
      el.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => { if (e.key === "Enter" || e.key === " ") { e.preventDefault(); map.fitBounds(VIEWS[key], { padding: 20, duration: 700 }); } });
    }
  }
  function styleInsets(newMode) {
    for (const { m, st, loaded } of Object.values(INSETS)) {
      if (!loaded) continue;
      m.setPaintProperty("land", "fill-color", TH.land);
      m.setPaintProperty("dist-fill", "fill-color", fillExpr());
      m.setPaintProperty("dist-line", "line-color", TH.border);
      m.setPaintProperty("sel-line", "line-color", TH.sel);
      if (newMode) m.getSource("dist").setData(distOf(st));
    }
  }
  function updateInsets() {
    const el = $("insets"); if (!el || measuring) return;
    const natZoom = (NAT ?? nationalCamera()).zoom;
    // hide once the real state is on screen (its centre is in view), so it never shows twice
    const W = map.getContainer().clientWidth, H = map.getContainer().clientHeight;
    const centreIn = (v) => { const p = map.project([(v[0][0] + v[1][0]) / 2, (v[0][1] + v[1][1]) / 2]); return p.x > 0 && p.x < W && p.y > 0 && p.y < H; };
    el.hidden = map.getZoom() > natZoom + 0.75 || centreIn(VIEWS.ak) || centreIn(VIEWS.hi);
    if (el.hidden) return;
    const fr = l48Frame(), FW = fr.x1 - fr.x0, FH = fr.base - fr.y0;
    for (const [key, ins] of Object.entries(INSETS)) {
      const L = LAYOUTS[PROJ][key], box = $("inset-" + key);
      const left = fr.x0 + L.x0 * FW, w = Math.round((L.x1 - L.x0) * FW), h = Math.round(L.h * FH);
      box.style.left = Math.round(left) + "px"; box.style.top = Math.round(fr.base - h) + "px";
      if (box.offsetWidth !== w || box.offsetHeight !== h) { box.style.width = w + "px"; box.style.height = h + "px"; ins.m.resize(); }
      fitInset(ins.m, INSET_FIT[key], w, h, INSET_PTS[key]);
    }
  }

  function updateLabels() {
    markers.forEach((m) => m.remove()); markers = [];
    if (map.getZoom() < 5.2) return;
    const b = map.getBounds(); let n = 0;
    for (const f of lblFC[S].features) {
      const [x, y] = f.geometry.coordinates;
      if (!b.contains([x, y])) continue;
      if (++n > 160) break;
      const el = document.createElement("div"); el.className = "lbl"; el.textContent = f.properties["d_" + S];
      markers.push(new maplibregl.Marker({ element: el }).setLngLat([x, y]).addTo(map));
    }
  }

  function wireMap() {
    const tip = $("tip");
    for (const L of ["zcta-fill", "zd-fill"]) map.on("mousemove", L, (e) => {
      const p = e.features[0].properties; const d = p["d_" + S]; const [dp, dev] = meta.results[S].districts[d];
      map.getCanvas().style.cursor = "pointer";
      tip.innerHTML = `<div><b>${zipLabel(p.zcta)}</b> · ${fmt(p.pop)} people</div><div class="t2">District <b>${d}</b> · ${fmt(dp)} <span class="pill ${devClass(dev)}">${devText(dev)}</span></div>`;
      tip.style.display = "block";
      const w = map.getContainer().clientWidth; const x = e.point.x + 14;
      tip.style.left = (x + 230 > w ? e.point.x - 240 : x) + "px"; tip.style.top = e.point.y + 14 + "px";
    });
    for (const L of ["zcta-fill", "zd-fill"]) map.on("mouseleave", L, () => { tip.style.display = "none"; map.getCanvas().style.cursor = ""; });
    for (const L of ["zcta-fill", "zd-fill"]) map.on("click", L, (e) => { const p = e.features[0].properties; pinnedZip = null; zipFilter = NONE; map.setFilter("zd-zip-line", NONE); select(p["d_" + S], false); });
    map.on("moveend", () => { updateLabels(); loadDetail(); refreshDetail(); });
    map.on("move", updateInsets); map.on("resize", () => { NAT = null; updateInsets(); });
    map.jumpTo(nationalCamera()); updateInsets();
    map.on("zoomend", refreshDetail);
    loadDetail(); refreshDetail();
  }

  // legend collapse, remembered in localStorage (collapsed by default, so it doesn't cover the East Coast at the national view)
  $("legend-toggle").addEventListener("click", () => {
    const lg = $("legend"); const c = lg.classList.toggle("collapsed");
    $("legend-toggle").setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!c));
    try { localStorage.setItem("zd-legend", c ? "0" : "1"); } catch (e) {}
  });
  try { if (localStorage.getItem("zd-legend") !== "1") { $("legend").classList.add("collapsed"); $("legend-toggle").setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false"); } } catch (e) {}
  function setProjection(p) {
    PROJ = p;
    try { localStorage.setItem("zd-proj", p); } catch (e) {}
    document.querySelectorAll(".proj button").forEach((b) => b.setAttribute("aria-checked", String(b.dataset.proj === p)));
    const wasNational = NAT && Math.abs(map.getZoom() - NAT.zoom) < 0.3;
    map.setProjection({ type: p });
    for (const { m } of Object.values(INSETS)) m.setProjection({ type: p });
    NAT = null;
    if (wasNational) map.jumpTo(nationalCamera());
    updateInsets();
  }
  document.querySelectorAll(".proj button").forEach((b) => { b.setAttribute("aria-checked", String(b.dataset.proj === PROJ)); b.addEventListener("click", () => setProjection(b.dataset.proj)); });
  document.querySelectorAll(".jump:not(.proj) button").forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => b.dataset.view === "l48" ? map.easeTo({ ...nationalCamera(), duration: 700 }) : map.fitBounds(VIEWS[b.dataset.view], { padding: 20, duration: 700 })));
  $("zipform").addEventListener("submit", (e) => { e.preventDefault(); const z = $("zipq").value.trim().padStart(5, "0"); if (meta) showZip(z); });
  window.addEventListener("hashchange", () => { const h = location.hash.slice(1); if (meta && h !== S && meta.strategies[h]) setStrategy(h); });
  load().catch((err) => { const l = $("loading"); if (l) l.textContent = "The map data didn't load (" + err.message + "). Reload the page to try again."; console.error(err); });
</script>
